<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance">
  <ScenTitle>María &amp; Victoria</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;FONT color=#ff0000&gt;&lt;FONT color=#000000&gt;&lt;FONT size=3&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;By:&lt;/STRONG&gt; Patricio Ortiz aka Patmanaut&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Argentina&amp;nbsp;vs. United Kingdom&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;Date:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt; 20th May 1982&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;Location:&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt; North of the Falkland Islands&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = "o" ns = "urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;B style="mso-bidi-font-weight: normal"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;Playable Sides&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/B&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;: Argentina&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-GB style="mso-ansi-language: EN-GB"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-US style="mso-ansi-language: EN-US"&gt;During the Malvinas / Falklands war, the Argentine navy could&amp;nbsp;deploy only&amp;nbsp;two operative submarines, the ARA San Luis&amp;nbsp;(Type 209 - 1100) and ARA Santa Fé (Type Balao - Guppy II) The other two submarines, ARA Salta, (209) was under routine maintenance, and ARA Santiago del Estero (Guppy II) was on decommisioning process.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-US style="mso-ansi-language: EN-US"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-US style="mso-ansi-language: EN-US"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-US style="mso-ansi-language: EN-US"&gt;The ARA Santa Fé had an active part disembarking the Amphibious Commando elements on April 2,&amp;nbsp;until its final combat at Grytviken harbor / Georgia island.&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-US style="mso-ansi-language: EN-US"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;
&lt;P class=MsoNormal style="MARGIN: 0cm 0cm 0pt"&gt;&lt;SPAN lang=EN-US style="mso-ansi-language: EN-US"&gt;Afterwards, the&amp;nbsp;only operational SSK left to confront the RN was ARA San Luis, who operated on several pre designated patrol areas. Most active zones where those north of the islands called Victoria (NW off cape Dolphin.) and María (NE, east off cape Dolphin.).&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
  <Complexity>1</Complexity>
  <Difficulty>3</Difficulty>
